  "result": "I stopped with the node failing the gate: the files as left return **WITNESS_FAIL** on the `blind` witness. That witness can't pass honestly, because the node planned it wrong. Everything else passes. A diagnostic run with a substitute `blind` witness returned `OK` across 18 witnesses. That substitute only passed for the wrong reason, so I put the planned `blind` back.\n\n**Why the node is wrong:**\n- `blind` masks `rel.bearing` and expects unknown.\n- Core computes `rel_bearing` from `kin.position` and `kin.heading` (`Core/Vocab/Atoms.lean:635`). The mask only removes a bearing the source measured, and a witness may not supply one Core can compute. On any trace with observed movement data, the mask therefore changes nothing, and `blind` comes out violated like `forbid`.\n- The pass concept `drv.interaction.overtake_pass` reads the same position and heading. Any trace that removes them leaves the pass undecided whether or not `rel.bearing` is masked, so the masked atom can never be what decides the verdict.\n- **What the plan should change:** mask `kin.position` (or `kin.heading`) in `blind`, since that removes the pass and the bearing together. Nothing else in the node needs to change.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n- I accidentally ran the gate once early, on the harness-written files, with its output thrown away; it may have used one run of the budget.\n- Run 2 gave WITNESS_FAIL, on `blind` only.\n- Run 3 was the diagnostic `OK`. Its `blind` was undecided only because b's position was missing, which breaks the rule that the masked atom must decide.\n\n**Choices the node left open:**\n- **When the pass is \"under way\":** the formula language has no operator for \"from the last observation where b was ahead to the one being judged\". The closest form also counts earlier observations where b was ahead with headings aligned while the subject moved (the approach). This makes the duty apply slightly more widely than the record states.\n- **No other vehicle:** \"With no other vehicle in the scene the duty is met\" is a separate branch of the applicability, so `permit` is compliant.\n- **Extra witness:** I added `branch_4` (violated): a working beacon that isn't flashing, but pupils aren't in class. The gate's adequacy check needed it.\n- **Judged instants:** every witness judges t = 12–19 s, so the 10-second look-back windows are fully covered.\n- I declared no narrowings.\n\nEverything is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
